{"decision":"GO-WITH-CONDITIONS","report":"Payload 16: no declared condition demonstrated false; no P0 found.\n\nNEW FINDINGS (annex)\n\nP1 — .claude/hooks/_lib/bash_indirect_guard.py:167\nThe command-substitution scanner treats quoted closing parentheses as terminators. The harmless command printf '%s\\n' \"$(git log -1 --format='(%h)')\" is blocked as bash_indirect_unparseable_shell. Confirmed through decide_command; disabling heuristics does not help. Minimal fix: track quotes, escapes and nesting when locating substitution boundaries.\n\nP1 — .claude/hooks/_lib/bash_indirect_guard.py:455\nEvery canonical-path operand following an interpreter's inline program is treated as a write target. Even python3 -c 'import sys; print(sys.argv[1])' PROTOCOL.md is blocked as bash_computed_canonical_target. Read-only file inspection is also blocked. Confirmed through decide_command, including with heuristics disabled. Minimal fix: require a recognized write operation before classifying interpreter operands as write targets.\n\nP1 — .claude/hooks/_lib/bash_indirect_guard.py:347\nStatic finding: recursive xargs/find processing calls _scan_segment directly without checking MAX_DEPTH. Deep launcher nesting can exhaust Python recursion while within the input caps. The exception reaches decisions_cli.py:243–248, which emits allow: an input-limit failure becomes fail-open. Minimal fix: enforce the depth ceiling at _scan_segment entry and return bash_indirect_limit.\n\nP2 follow-ups\n\nP2 — .claude/hooks/_lib/bash_indirect_telemetry.py:53\nA pre-existing symlink at bash-indirect-disabled redirects marker creation outside the audit directory. O_EXCL protects the final filename, not its parent; the resulting files are empty markers, without overwriting existing files. Minimal fix: validate and open the marker directory without following symlinks, then create markers relative to its directory descriptor.\n\nValidation: both false blocks disappear when only the new scanner is disabled. Python 3.9 syntax checks passed for the new scanner, telemetry and canonical binding/decisions files. Static audit/canonical binding review found no concrete regression. Audit emission was stubbed during decision probes; no files were modified. Redaction artifacts were excluded.","sentence":"The findings warrant follow-up, but this payload establishes neither a false declared condition nor a P0."}
